# =============================================================================
# openpi LIBERO eval harness patch — pi0.5 (and pi0-FAST) on the customized
# libero_object_unseen* suites
# =============================================================================
#
# WHAT THIS IS
#   A git patch for the openpi LIBERO evaluation client. It teaches the stock
#   harness to (a) run our custom object-swapped suites, (b) run an arbitrary
#   subset of task ids (for sharding across GPUs), (c) write a structured,
#   crash-safe results JSON, and (d) survive robosuite RandomizationErrors
#   instead of dying mid-run. Same client is used for pi0.5 and pi0-FAST — only
#   the served checkpoint and --model_name differ.
#
# UPSTREAM BASE (apply on top of exactly this)
#   repo   : https://github.com/Physical-Intelligence/openpi.git
#   branch : main
#   commit : 15a9616a00943ada6c20a0f158e3adb39df2ccac
#            ("update output objects to support batching (#975)")
#   If HEAD differs, `git apply` may reject hunks; check out the commit above
#   first, or apply with `patch -p1` (fuzzier) and eyeball the result.
#
# FILES TOUCHED
#   examples/libero/main.py      <- the real work (new args, results JSON,
#                                    RandomizationError retries/skip, MAX_STEPS
#                                    table incl. the unseen suites, unique
#                                    per-episode video names)
#   examples/libero/Dockerfile   <- config.yaml written via printf (heredoc was
#                                    brittle); functional no-op
#   examples/libero/compose.yml  <- pin the GPU with ${GPU_ID:-0} instead of
#                                    count:1, so two containers can target
#                                    different physical GPUs for sharded runs
#
# HOW TO APPLY (on the new machine)
#   git clone https://github.com/Physical-Intelligence/openpi.git
#   cd openpi
#   git checkout 15a9616a00943ada6c20a0f158e3adb39df2ccac
#   git apply /path/to/openpi_pi05_libero_eval.patch      # or: patch -p1 < ...
#   # verify: git apply --check /path/to/openpi_pi05_libero_eval.patch
#
# PREREQUISITE — the suites must be registered in the env you run this in
#   The client calls `benchmark.get_benchmark_dict()[args.task_suite_name]`.
#   For "libero_object_unseen" / "libero_object_unseen_full" to resolve, the
#   CUSTOMIZED LIBERO fork must be the installed `libero` package:
#       repo : https://github.com/leo5470/LIBERO.git
#       note : the unseen + unseen_full suites live on the branches that still
#              contain them (they were later removed on cosmos-predict2.5-eval,
#              which keeps only libero_object_unseen_stockbg). Check out a branch
#              that has the suite you want, and make sure its bddl_files/,
#              init_files/, manifest.json and converted assets/ are present and
#              pointed at by ~/.libero/config.yaml.
#   Stock suites (libero_object, etc.) work with an unmodified LIBERO.
#
# HOW TO RUN (two processes: policy server + this client)
#   1) Serve the checkpoint (separate openpi server process), e.g. pi05_libero.
#   2) Run this client. New/changed flags:
#        --task_suite_name   libero_object_unseen_full   # or _unseen / _stockbg / stock
#        --task_ids          "0,2,4,..."   # optional subset; omit = all tasks.
#                                          # We sharded by even/odd ids across 2 GPUs.
#        --num_trials_per_task 10          # finals used 10; upstream default is 50
#        --seed              7             # finals seed
#        --model_name        pi05_libero   # stamped into results JSON + filename
#        --results_out_path  /path/to/eval_results/full   # dir for incremental JSON
#        --save_videos       failures      # all | failures | none
#        --video_out_path    /path/to/videos
#   Example:
#     python examples/libero/main.py \
#       --task_suite_name libero_object_unseen_full \
#       --num_trials_per_task 10 --seed 7 \
#       --model_name pi05_libero \
#       --results_out_path /tmp2/leocheng/eval_results/full \
#       --task_ids "$(seq -s, 0 2 1556)"        # even ids -> GPU0 lane, etc.
#
# RESULTS FORMAT (one file per run, rewritten atomically after every task)
#   <results_out_path>/<model_name>_<suite>_trials<N>_seed<S>.json
#   {model, suite, num_trials_per_task, seed, max_steps,
#    total_episodes, total_successes,
#    tasks:[{task_id, task_name, language, episodes, successes,
#            episode_results:[{episode_idx, success, steps}], error?}]}
#   A task that could not build/reset carries an "error" tag and 0 episodes
#   (values: randomization_error_env_build / randomization_error_episode_reset).
#   Feed these files to LIBERO fork scripts/aggregate_unseen_eval.py together
#   with the suite's manifest.json to get per-category success-rate CSVs.
#
# GOTCHAS worth re-deriving on the new box
#   * MAX_STEPS for the unseen suites = 280 (they reuse the libero_object task
#     design). New suites you add must be inserted into the MAX_STEPS table or
#     the client raises "Unknown task suite".
#   * env.seed() affects object positions even with a fixed init state, so the
#     RandomizationError retry loop just resamples — the state is overwritten by
#     set_init_state() right after, so retrying is safe.
#   * Reference numbers produced by this harness (finals, seed 7):
#     pi0.5  full 1,421-task suite = 29.1% ; 92-task = 46.6%.
#     pi0-FAST full = 15.9%.  (sanity check a re-run against these.)
#
# Source working tree this diff was captured from:
#   /tmp2/leocheng/PhysicalIntelligence/openpi  (uncommitted changes, 2026-07-24)
# =============================================================================

